## Data licensing notes

The source code in `src/` and the documentation in `docs/` are MIT licensed.

The datasets under `data/` contain metadata only:

- `data/ledger.jsonl` — post titles, URLs, timestamps, point counts, and
  author identifiers from Hacker News, retrieved via the public Algolia
  search API. Post titles are short factual descriptions of a product and are
  reproduced under the Hacker News Terms of Use, which permit linking and
  short quoted excerpts. Titles are not redistributed in bulk as a substitute
  for the original source; every row carries the HN objectID so any entry can
  be traced to its original post.
- `data/repo_status.jsonl` and `data/liveness.jsonl` — factual metadata about
  public GitHub repositories and public DNS/HTTP status, obtained from
  documented public APIs.
- `data/days/` — raw per-day API responses, retained for reproducibility.

No personal data beyond public GitHub account identifiers and public HN
usernames is collected or redistributed. Product URLs are collected because
they are the subject of the dataset; the dataset's purpose is to measure
whether those products are still operating.
